## Task

Review the merged implementation and confirm each of the following. Post a comment on THIS issue with findings for (i), (ii), (iii) marking each PASS or FAIL with brief evidence.

(i) State directory safety: $CB_HOME/run/state/<id>/ is created safely (mkdir -p or equivalent) with correct permissions/ownership. Confirm no race-on-first-write risk -- i.e., the launcher tick model guarantees single-writer-per-leaf-id (only one launcher process acts on a given leaf id at a time).

(ii) Config documentation: CB_INFRA_RETRY_CAP, CB_INFRA_BACKOFF_BASE, and CB_INFRA_BACKOFF_MULT are all present in reference/runtime/run-env.sh with export and default values, following the same pattern as CB_REWORK_CAP (lines 74-75). Confirm the comment header for each var describes its semantics.

(iii) Lock-contention analysis: Confirm that no two launcher processes can concurrently write to $STATE/<id>/infra_attempt. The single-launcher-process model (flock on launcher.lock, cmd_once path) is the write-serialization guarantee -- confirm it holds, OR document any edge case (e.g., concurrent re-dispatch vs tick) and state whether explicit per-file locking is needed.

